# The same brief, answered by asking what the reactor is actually for.
#
# Two exchangers can take 500 heat a tick and no more, so a reactor at full
# throttle is heating the sky with the other half. Turn it down to 40% and the
# plant makes the same power on a third of the fuel, wastes nothing, and fits
# on a plot a quarter the size of 02-more-of-everything.

machine "Compact"

reactor   R1  at 0,0  throttle 40

exchanger HX1 at 4,0
turbine   T1  at 7,0
generator G1  at 10,0

exchanger HX2 at 4,3
turbine   T2  at 7,3
generator G2  at 10,3

pump      W1  at 0,4

wire R1.heat -> HX1.heat
wire R1.heat -> HX2.heat
wire W1.water -> HX1.water
wire W1.water -> HX2.water
wire HX1.steam -> T1.steam
wire HX2.steam -> T2.steam
wire T1.rotary -> G1.rotary
wire T2.rotary -> G2.rotary
